id: pm-qz1k
title: "Typed parameter binding manifests: declare preset parameters once, resolve across settings, templates and seeds"
description: "From the 2026-10-21 fleet backlog audit item 2. Declare required preset parameters once in a typed manifest and resolve them consistently through settings, templates and seeds, returning unanswered choices before installation. Acceptance: (1) one supplied project parameter reaches every declared occurrence; (2) unknown/missing bindings refuse before any write; (3) secret values cannot enter generated public seed prose. Deliver typed SDK surface + CLI flags, compact TOON/JSON output, typed refusals with remedies, docs, property tests and real-data validation on a read-only copy of a public fleet tracker in a non-git temp dir."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[8]: authoring,bindings,"gh:unbraind/pm-presets#170","gh:unbraind/pm-presets#171","gh:unbraind/pm-presets#173",parameters,presets,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-27T12:08:56.144Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T00:55:12.596Z"
author: pi-agent
comments[26]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T12:09:22.235Z",pi-agent,"Overlap check (re-run 2026-10-27 against pm CLI 2026.10.20 SDK and sibling packages): (a) pm-cli SDK has no parameter/interpolation capability — grep over the installed SDK declarations shows settings mutations are literal audited patches (mutateWorkspaceSettings), templates are literal option maps (loadCreateTemplateOptions/runTemplatesShow), client.create takes literal fields; no 'parameter|interpolat|substitut' matches in templates/workspace-contracts/schema declarations. (b) gh search issues --repo unbraind/pm-cli 'parameter binding'/'preset parameter'/'template parameter': no open upstream work. (c) Fleet sibling scan (src/docs) for parameter-binding/interpolation features: no hits. (d) In-package status: presets accept only a few CLI overrides (--prefix, --force, --dry-run, --replace, --with-seeds) and upgrades of known settings; seed and template values are static literals. Conclusion: no overlap — this adds parameter propagation as an explicit authoring contract while the resolved native fields are still validated by the existing core path (preset validation + the host's audited settings mutation), so no core schema change is required."
  "2026-10-27T14:07:02.392Z",pi-agent,"Revert proof (2026-10-27): behaviourally reverted the parameter handling in applyPreset (resolution disabled; raw binding syntax passes through) and re-ran the focused new tests: 8 of 11 fail (one-value-reaches-every-occurrence, default resolution, refusal-before-writes, params-file, diff parity, dry-run, property round-trip, concurrent applies). Restored the implementation: 8/8 params-cli tests pass again. Full suite before the gate: 238 tests pass, 0 fail (node --test --test-concurrency=2 on a saturated 4-core host)."
  "2026-10-27T14:56:36.277Z",pi-agent,"Real-data validation (2026-10-27), on byte-identical temp copies of this repository's public pm tracker in non-git temp dirs (GIT_CEILING set; the repo tracker itself was never touched): (1) READ-ONLY copy (chmod a-w): parameterized diff with projectKey=acme compared 13 settings leaves -> 1 add, 6 change, id_prefix 'acme-' vs stored 'pm-'; default-resolution diff reported the 'road-' default; supplying an undeclared parameter refused with typed code unknown_parameter listing the declared parameter; a full-file digest proved every tracker byte unchanged afterwards. (2) Writable temp copy: dry-run apply resolved 1 parameter into 3 binding occurrences (id_prefix + two template bodies, all showing acme); an invalid value (uppercase) refused with invalid_value before any write; a real --with-seeds apply read back through the SDK as id_prefix 'acme-', 2/2 template bodies carrying the occurrence, seed item titled 'Define the acme first roadmap initiative', 85 items after seeding (84 tracked items + 1 seed). (3) Note: the audited settings mutation takes a workspace-history lock, so a dry-run apply against the read-only copy refuses with a lock conflict - expected host behavior, mirrored by presets diff which reads without locks."
  "2026-10-27T15:05:24.901Z",pi-agent,"Gate evidence (2026-10-27): full local suite node --test tests/*.test.ts: 241 tests, 241 pass, 0 fail. Coverage gate (taskset 2 CPUs): 241 tests pass, coverage 100.00% lines / 100.00% branches / 100.00% functions over every source file (src/params.ts fully covered: 212/212 branches). Property test (seeded, deterministic, PM_PRESETS_PROPERTY_SEED): 520 random operation sequences on real non-git temp trackers (fresh applies, replays of older inputs, whitespace-padded values, CRLF/control/unicode/overlong refusals with byte-identical no-write proofs, ambient session focus never inherited as a seed parent, export/diff previews agreeing with the reference model, all state read back through the SDK), plus 600 synthetic manifest resolutions and one concurrent-interleaving test (2 applies + 2 seed runs race on one tracker; final state consistent with some serial order, no unresolved binding syntax survives). The full CI release gate (npm + bun) is the remaining full-gate evidence."
  "2026-10-27T15:08:05.600Z",pi-agent,"PR opened for review (not draft): https://github.com/unbraind/pm-presets/pull/170 on branch feat/typed-parameter-binding-manifests. Commit 24492dc carries the src/dist/tests/docs changes together with this pm item and its history. Full-gate evidence is the CI release gate (npm + bun) on the PR."
  "2026-10-27T18:11:01.052Z",pi-agent,"CI release gate PASSED (2026-10-27): https://github.com/unbraind/pm-presets/actions/runs/40528008693 - npm run release:check: 241 tests / 241 pass / 0 fail, coverage-gate '26 source file(s) reported, thresholds met' (100% lines/branches/functions), prod audit, pack dry-run, changelog check and release verifiers all green; bun run release:check: 241 tests / 241 pass / 0 fail, same coverage gate. Also passing on the PR: test matrix (node 22 and 26), windows-prepare-lifecycle, codeql, Hound, CodeRabbit. All checks green on https://github.com/unbraind/pm-presets/pull/170."
  "2026-10-27T19:07:00.000Z",pi-agent,"Re-review round 1 (2026-10-27): addressing all five blocking findings class-wide: (1) secret redaction in EVERY emitted surface (dry-run patch dump, diff results); (2) catalog/read surfaces become declaration-mode (required-no-default parameters no longer break show/apply-with-param; views flag unanswered choices and only apply/parameterized-diff refuse); (3) apply pre-validates seed bindings BEFORE the setup handler writes anything; (4) parameter values resolved ONCE at the apply boundary and threaded through settings, templates and seeds (no params-file re-read); (5) settings mutation + template writes serialized under a workspace-scoped apply lock. Merged origin/main (deps bump to pm-cli 2026.10.23) first; merge history verified as byte-identical prefix; re-installed the pinned host."
  "2026-10-27T23:54:01.544Z",pi-agent,"Re-review round 1 fixes (2026-10-27) — all five blocking findings addressed class-wide, each with an adversarial test that fails on behavioural revert: (1) SECRETS NEVER ENTER EMITTED OUTPUT: the dry-run patch dump and BOTH sides of every diff settings entry now redact resolved secret values via one primitive (redactSecretValues); summary lines were already redacted; read surfaces (show/list) keep secret occurrences authored because declaration mode never resolves secrets; the ONLY place a secret lands is the private settings.json an apply writes. Revert proof: removing the dry-run dump redaction fails 'dry-run apply redacts secret values from every emitted line'; removing the diff redaction fails 'diff results redact secret values on both sides'. (2) DECLARATIONS BEFORE ANSWERS: catalog/read surfaces resolve leniently (collectParameterValues) and never refuse for unanswered parameters (views flag unanswered, authored occurrences survive); apply and the parameterized diff preview keep strict refusals with the typed remedy; the unified apply now passes supplied values into the definition lookup, so --param answers questions instead of being ignored. Revert proof: restoring strict catalog resolution fails 6 tests (projection, show-with-unanswered, apply-with-param, seed pre-validation, boundary). (3) VALIDATE BEFORE ANY SIDE EFFECT: the unified apply resolves the preset id, every parameter AND the seed bindings at ONE boundary (resolvePresetApplication) before the setup handler runs; a malformed or secret seed binding refuses with settings and templates untouched. Revert proof: restoring post-handler validation fails both seed pre-write tests. (4) RESOLVE ONCE, THREAD EVERYWHERE: apply reads flags/params file exactly once, then threads the effective values through the handler (contextWithResolvedParameters) and into seed creation; applyPreset re-validates injected values (assertResolvedParameterValues) instead of re-reading input. Revert proof: restoring the re-read in the handler fails the injection and boundary tests. (5) CONSISTENT MULTI-PART WRITES: real applies hold a workspace-scoped O_EXCL lock (locks/pm-presets-apply.lock, owner token, stale steal, poll-then-refuse) across the audited settings mutation AND the template writes; dry-runs skip the lock (read-only trackers keep failing only on host locks); release deletes only a file that still carries the owner's token. Revert proof: removing the lock fails the held-lock serialization test (and the concurrent property test now asserts FULL consistency: surviving templates describe the same invocation as the surviving id_prefix). Also wrapped stack plan parameter refusals... removed again as unreachable — stack's candidates loop runs before its try block, so bundled-seed parameter refusals already surface as typed ParameterRefusals; no unreachable wrap shipped."
  "2026-10-28T00:00:34.719Z",pi-agent,"Re-review fixes CI gate PASSED (2026-10-27, commit 38c33ad): https://github.com/unbraind/pm-presets/actions/runs/40605346143 - npm run release:check: 258 tests / 258 pass / 0 fail, coverage-gate '27 source file(s) reported, thresholds met' (100% lines/branches/functions), audit/pack/changelog/verifiers green; bun run release:check: 258 tests / 258 pass / 0 fail, same coverage gate. Also green on the PR: test matrix (node 22/26), windows-prepare-lifecycle, codeql, CodeQL, Hound, CodeRabbit. All checks green on https://github.com/unbraind/pm-presets/pull/170."
  "2026-10-28T22:08:21.475Z",codex-sol,"Continuing the published PR after reading its body and tracker evidence. Merged origin/main with two parents before implementation. Review rules: redact secret-bearing locations on both sides of rotation and before output encoding; normalize defaults and supplied values identically; resolve defaults at every seed consumer. Will audit SDK and CLI read/write/JSON/TOON paths, reuse applicable unpublished fixes without changing the previous worktree, add class-level adversarial properties and revert proofs, run focused tests then full gates with at most two workers, and verify packed npm/Bun consumers. Issues #171 and #173 are in this PR and included. No additional non-blocking findings appear in the supplied review or published inline reviews."
  "2026-10-28T22:10:46.738Z",codex-sol,"Class audit: settings dry-run was the only post-serialization value redaction; both diff command registrations share computeParameterizedDiff. Authored secret paths now travel on projected definitions so low-level computePresetDiff also hides rotated stored values of any JSON shape; direct SDK definitions infer sensitive scalar/array leaves from resolved secrets. Nested defense-in-depth redaction happens before JSON/TOON encoding. Seed consumers plan, stack, planSeeds, seedPresetItems and runPresetSeeds all use resolvedSeedsForPreset, which now collects manifest defaults without rereading files. Default collection and parameter views use the same normalization/constraints as supplied inputs, and injected resolutions reject noncanonical values instead of validating trimmed values then using raw ones. Added deterministic properties over Unicode whitespace, enum/pattern length boundaries, quote/backslash/Unicode/lone-surrogate secrets, rotations and nested settings shapes."
  "2026-10-28T22:17:17.351Z",codex-sol,"Revert proof: each mutation was applied alone, ran the matching adversarial property in tests/params-review.test.ts, then was restored in a finally block. All five mutations failed with exit 1: rotation (remove provenance and sensitive-leaf redaction); encoding (serialize before value redaction); seed-defaults (use supplied-only seed values); default-normalization (assign raw defaults); injected-normalization (accept noncanonical resolved values). Focused tracker-run command passed 50/50 with zero skips, including packed npm tarball execution under Node and Bun through both diff registrations, both JSON/TOON renderers, setup/apply dry-runs, stack identity/ownership and normalized show defaults. Two additional focused checks pass for parameterless seed validation and helper immutability. Strict tracker health passes with the current host; the older pinned SDK host sees a globally installed pm-github version skew, with no tracked extension implicated. Full release gates now running with two CPU affinity."
  "2026-10-28T22:29:15.845Z",codex-sol,"The full npm run exposed two existing SDK partial-result tests failing after the extra parameterless-seed guard eagerly invoked accessors. Stopped that already-failed gate to repair the regression. The guard now validates only enumerable data descriptors and returns original seeds, so native create still catches each accessor failure in order; original tests are unchanged. Added a no-accessor/non-enumerable regression alongside the undeclared-binding guard. The coverage runner now explicitly uses --test-concurrency=2 so local and CI release gates retain the requested bound independently of CPU count. Will rerun focused seeds/parameters, coverage, and both full release gates."
  "2026-10-28T22:31:08.115Z",codex-sol,"Compatibility repair verified: original SDK seed partial-result/accessor tests and all focused seed/parameter tests pass (34/34). A focused coverage run across params.ts, diff.ts and seeds.ts passes 60/60, with 100.00% lines, branches and functions for all three files. Command: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --experimental-test-coverage --test-coverage-include=src/params.ts --test-coverage-include=src/diff.ts --test-coverage-include=src/seeds.ts tests/params.test.ts tests/params-review.test.ts tests/seeds.test.ts tests/diff.test.ts. Both full release gates are being rerun on the repaired source with the explicit two-worker runner."
  "2026-10-28T22:42:47.233Z",codex-sol,"Final surface audit: catalog projections retain authored secret locations; computePresetDiff protects them even without supplied values, while computeParameterizedDiff also infers sensitive leaves for hand-built SDK definitions and redacts nested output values before rendering. Both diff registrations, normal JSON/TOON and strict rendering share that result. Setup aliases and unified apply share the pre-serialization dry-run path; plan, stack, seed plans and seed writes share the normalized seed resolver. Explicit workspace export and upgrade recovery artifacts are native configuration snapshots without parameter inputs; simulation uses isolated synthetic trackers. No second post-serialization parameter-redaction call was found. Packed regression fixtures use synthetic credentials only and never alter package source or the tracked project."
  "2026-10-28T22:49:34.756Z",codex-sol,"Final npm release:check PASSED after the compatibility repair: 270 tests, 270 pass, zero failures/skips/cancellations; coverage 100.00% lines / 100.00% branches / 100.00% functions, all 27 gated source files reported. Typecheck, complete docstring gate, production audit, package dry-run, changelog check, publish-attestation verifier and version-derived changelog-date verifier all passed. Runner explicitly caps test concurrency at 2; scheduler affinity was widened during the long stack model without changing tests or worker count. The full Bun release gate is now running on the same source."
  "2026-10-28T23:00:09.779Z",codex-sol,"Final source review found an additional output-contract class in the continuation: redacting the entire diff tree could replace public control metadata when a secret equals a status, path component or identifier (for example change or match). Redaction is now limited to settings payload values; sensitive locations still redact both sides wholesale, including rotations and nested values. Added a property over all statuses and representative identifier/key collisions that preserves paths, statuses, preset identity, template/item-type metadata and counts while asserting both credential values are hidden. Stopped the in-progress Bun gate to repair this before publication; prior 270-test npm evidence is a checkpoint, and both complete gates will be rerun on the corrected source."
  "2026-10-28T23:02:28.727Z",codex-sol,"Final focused verification: 61/61 tests pass, zero skips; params.ts, diff.ts and seeds.ts each retain 100.00% lines/branches/functions. Repeated every behavioural revert on the corrected source: rotation, serialization-before-redaction, seed defaults, raw-default normalization, injected-value normalization and control-metadata redaction all fail with exit 1 under their matching adversarial property. All six mutations were restored in finally blocks. Native diff control fields now remain stable for valid secrets equal to add/change/match, preset identifiers, path/key names or the redaction marker. Full npm and Bun release gates are running sequentially with an explicit maximum of two test workers. The pinned-host strict health check also passed with isolated user configuration, confirming the earlier global-extension skew was environmental."
  "2026-10-28T23:18:08.592Z",codex-sol,"Corrected-source npm release:check PASSED completely: 271 tests, 271 pass, no failures/skips/cancellations; 100.00% lines/branches/functions across all 27 gated source files. Typecheck, docstrings, production audit, package dry-run, changelog check and both release verifiers passed. This supersedes the earlier 270-test checkpoint and includes the output-control collision property. The final Bun release gate is now running on this unchanged source with test concurrency capped at two."
  "2026-10-28T23:33:53.363Z",codex-sol,"Completion evidence for https://github.com/unbraind/pm-presets/pull/170: all three reported blocking classes and issues #171/#173 are addressed across shared SDK/CLI paths. Final npm run release:check and bun run release:check both PASSED: 271/271 tests each, zero failures/skips/cancellations, 100.00% lines/branches/functions across all 27 gated source files. Typecheck, docstrings, production audit, package contents, changelog and both release verifiers passed in both gates. Packed tarball consumers exercise Node and Bun, both diff forms and JSON/TOON, setup/apply dry-runs, normalized show defaults and stack seed ownership in non-git trackers. All six isolated behavioural reverts fail their corresponding properties; fixes restored. Existing tests and coverage thresholds were preserved. Existing PM history remains an exact byte prefix. The original unpublished worktree remains untouched. No additional non-blocking finding was supplied or found in the published inline reviews. Releasing this claim for orchestrator verification; CI and independent re-review remain after push, and this item stays in progress."
  "2026-10-28T23:45:24.003Z",codex-sol,"Round 3 continuation: clean worktree and published head ce38e2e verified; origin/main is already an ancestor, so no merge is needed. Reclaimed this item. Rules: a contender must never remove a lock generation it did not observe, and file-boundary I/O errors must become stable privacy-safe typed refusals before any tracker write. Auditing acquisition, stale recovery and release as one ownership protocol, plus every params-file SDK/CLI reader, both diff forms and setup/apply paths. Will preserve prior fixes, add deterministic adversarial interleavings and file-fault properties with revert proofs, run focused tests then both full gates at no more than two workers, push and release without closing. No additional non-blocking finding appears in the supplied round or published inline comments."
  "2026-10-29T00:10:39.390Z",codex-sol,"Class design: a token comparison followed by unlink is still a TOCTOU race. Every apply now holds a unique immutable admission claim across the existing token-file publication, stale recovery, settings/templates mutation and release. Contenders withdraw before waiting; recovery deletes only the exact observed dead claim pathname, never a shared replacement pathname. The claims directory is retained to avoid directory-generation ABA. Automatic recovery requires matching verified kernel/PID namespace and a PID proven absent; live or unverifiable owners fail closed, including long-running applies. This preserves the existing token-file protocol and every old assertion. All public JSON artifact readers now share descriptor-bound regular-file reads with byte limits; params maps I/O faults to invalid_params_file/exit 2 and upgrade/plan/stack keep their existing typed refusals. Both paramsFile and params-file SDK spellings use that single boundary. Focused tests cover every open/stat/read/close fault, file growth/short reads, descriptor cleanup, all setup/apply/diff entry points, and deterministic cross-process stale/release interleavings paused immediately before unlink."
  "2026-10-29T00:18:52.134Z",codex-sol,"Round 3 revert proof: removing only the admission fence (leaving token comparisons and the original lock logic) fails BOTH independent-process properties: stale takeover admits overlapping native writes, and delayed release unlinks the replacement generation (ENOENT while that owner is held). Removing only params-file I/O translation fails the file-fault property with raw ENOENT instead of invalid_params_file. Both mutations exited 1 and were restored in finally blocks. The expanded focused run passed 53/53 before splitting stale/release into independent tests; the subsequent core coverage run passed 52/52 and measured 100.00% lines/branches/functions for both new modules. Only pre-existing malformed-binding branches were outside that focused subset; the unchanged full gate remains 100% in every dimension. Existing assertions and thresholds are preserved. The current strengthened focused command is linked and will be executed through pm before both full release gates."
  "2026-10-29T00:25:32.575Z",codex-sol,"Current round 3 focused command passed through pm test --run --only-last --progress --timeout 1200: 54/54 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations. This includes independently reported stale-takeover and delayed-release tests, actual native field/template coherence after handoff, immutable dead-claim replacement recovery, live/foreign/unverifiable ownership, all file I/O fault stages, all SDK setup/apply/diff paths, and the packed Node/Bun JSON/TOON matrix. Both new modules measured 100.00% lines/branches/functions in focused coverage; full thresholds remain configured at 100% and will now be measured across all sources. Both full release gates are running sequentially with the existing explicit two-worker cap."
  "2026-10-29T00:38:09.635Z",codex-sol,"Round 3 npm run release:check PASSED completely: 280 tests, 280 pass, zero failures/skips/cancellations; 100.00% lines, branches and functions across all 29 gated source files, including both new modules. Typecheck, 77-file/194-declaration docstring gate, production audit, npm package dry-run, changelog check and both release verifiers passed. The full Bun gate is now running on the same unchanged source. The 100% measurements here supersede the earlier focused-subset coverage; no threshold or existing assertion was reduced."
  "2026-10-29T00:55:10.885Z",codex-sol,"Round 3 completion for https://github.com/unbraind/pm-presets/pull/170: npm run release:check AND bun run release:check both PASSED on the unchanged corrected source: 280/280 tests each, zero failures/skips/cancellations; 100.00% lines, branches and functions over all 29 gated source files. Typecheck, complete docstrings, production audit, package dry-run, changelog and both release verifiers passed in both gates. Focused pm-run evidence is 54/54. Behavioral reversions produce two ownership-race failures (actual overlapping native writes and deletion of the replacement generation) and one raw-ENOENT refusal failure; fixes restored. Packed Node/Bun consumers cover both output formats, all seven setup aliases, unified apply, both diff forms and independent-process ownership handoffs on non-git trackers. Prior fixes and assertions are preserved. Recovery intentionally refuses to reap unverifiable owners; confirmed manual inspection is required when a kernel/PID namespace cannot be verified. Releasing the claim for orchestrator CI/re-review verification; item remains in progress and is not closed."
